.TH logname 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
logname \- print the login name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logname
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B logname
prints the name in
.B /etc/passwd
of the
.I real
user id, which is the one you logged in as and does not change when
.BR su (1)
does.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
1, and no output, if the real uid is not in
.BR /etc/passwd .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR whoami (1),
.BR id (1)
